    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0084" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p2/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119–Control (Japan)/3–149</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Paul H. Nitze, Deputy to the Assistant
                        Secretary of State for Economic Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Thorp</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Director of the Office of Far Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-03-01">March 1, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I suggest that you read the attached memorandum<anchor n="1" xml:id="d36-f1"/> on
                    “The Hutchinson Reports on the Japanese Deconcentration Program” which appears
                    to me to make a great deal of sense.</p>


                <xi:include href="d36-a1.xml" xpointer="d36-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
